rca of the issue:
has_permission() in /app/backend/services/auth.py line 71-75:

    def has_permission(user: dict, permission: str) -> bool:
        if user.get('role') == 'super_admin':
            return True
        return permission in user.get('permissions', [])

This only reads user['permissions']. The permissions-admin endpoint PUT /api/permissions/users/{email}/overrides writes to user['extra_pages'] / user['denied_pages'] and never touches user['permissions']. /warehouse/adjust → _can_manage → has_permission(user, 'warehouse_manage') therefore returns False even after the override is set to ['warehouse_manage']. Confirmed via /permissions/me: warehouse_manage IS in effective 'pages' but adjust still 403s.

Reproduction:
1. POST /api/admin/users (staff role)
2. PUT /api/permissions/users/{email}/overrides body {"extra_pages":["warehouse_manage"]}
3. Login as that staff.
4. POST /api/warehouse/adjust {product_id, mode:'set', quantity:50, reason:'stocktake_correction'} → 403.

Mitigation: Update has_permission to compute effective pages using the same merge as /permissions/me (role_pages ∪ extra_pages − denied_pages), OR update warehouse._can_manage to call the merged-computation helper directly.
